{"page":28901,"revision":1373607912,"ref":"o14","kind":"statement/axiom","cue":"named-heading","strength":"normal","name":"Verification of group axioms","section":"Group properties and special elements > Verification of group axioms","section_anchor":"Verification_of_group_axioms","span":[7124,8026],"text":"### Verification of group axioms\nTo check that the symmetric group on a set X is indeed a group, it is necessary to verify the group axioms of closure, associativity, identity, and inverses.\n- The operation of function composition is closed in the set of permutations of the given set X.\n- Function composition is always associative.\n- The trivial bijection that assigns each element of X to itself serves as an identity for the group.\n- Every bijection has an inverse function that undoes its action, and thus each element of a symmetric group does have an inverse which is a permutation too.","links":[{"title":"Group (mathematics)"},{"title":"Inverse function"}],"citations":["o15"],"hash":"sha256:7ecba3d7f90ac18432fa0a7b59b80a77cd5b6d5c83e22e99f0cb2769f1e4be9f","extractor":"m2/v0.3.8"}
